Subject: [PATCH 10/14] feat(trace): Centerline Join gaps control (ADR-396)

Centerline now shows a Join gaps setting (pixels, default 3) where the
filled styles show Ignore Less Than. It sets how close two line ends must
be, while pointing toward each other, for the tracer to join them into one
line; 0 leaves gaps open. The value carries over like other adjustments:
it applies only while Centerline is selected, is listed as "Not used by"
under other styles, counts toward "Settings edited", and Reset trace
settings restores the preset's 3.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
